  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ResCoordDisc 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "A group of medical students is touring the research lab, and one of
    them notices you flipping through a binder labeled \u201Csample logs\u201D while
    sorting through digital files at a nearby computer. The staff member introduces
    you to the students as the research coordinator, explaining that you help organize
    information so the research team can easily find what they need when preparing
    for future studies.\n\nIn this situation, what role does the research coordinator
    play?"
  explanation: "In the discovery stage, research coordinators help with organization
    and documentation \u2014 not lab testing or drug/treatment design. Their work
    ensures early findings can move smoothly into preclinical testing later. By keeping
    information clear and well-tracked, they help the research team avoid delays
    or confusion as the research project advances."
  correctAnswer: "D: Ensuring the research team\u2019s early data and materials are
    ready for later research steps"
  incorrectAnswer1: 'A: Conducting lab experiments to test how a new treatment works
    in mice'
  incorrectAnswer2: 'B: Designing chemical structures of new cancer drugs/treatments'
  incorrectAnswer3: 'C: Using lab data to determine which patients will receive the
    new treatment'
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
